      "explanation": "A shuffled split puts hour t-1 and hour t+1 in training while hour t is in test, so with lag features the model has effectively already seen the answer. That makes it invalid here whatever it scores -- and on this series it does not even flatter the result, which is worth stating plainly rather than repeating the assumption. The single chronological tail is leak-free but lands on a flat, quiet fortnight and reports a meaninglessly low error. Rolling-origin is what the model card, /metrics and every response carry."
